#: Score/AnalysisResultDetailAdapter.php:113
msgid "DMARC (Domain-based Message Authentication, Reporting, and Conformance) ties SPF and DKIM together, providing a policy framework for these protocols."
msgstr ""

#: Score/AnalysisResultDetailAdapter.php:115
msgid "SPF (Sender Policy Framework) verifies that your emails are sent from authorized servers."
msgstr ""

#: Score/AnalysisResultDetailAdapter.php:117
msgid "DKIM (DomainKeys Identified Mail) adds a digital signature to your emails, ensuring they haven't been tampered with."
msgstr ""

#: Score/AnalysisResultDetailAdapter.php:119
msgid "Domain age impacts reputation; older domains are more trusted due to established presence and credibility. Newer domains lack trust and authority as they haven't built reputation or audience yet."
msgstr ""

#: Score/AnalysisResultDetailAdapter.php:121
msgid "BIMI shows logos in emails, using DNS records. It helps fighting phishing by enhancing brand recognition."
msgstr ""

#: Score/AnalysisResultDetailAdapter.php:123
msgid "MX records designate recipient mail servers for a domain. It's not enough for a sender to just be able to send emails; they also need to receive them."
msgstr ""

#: Score/AnalysisResultDetailAdapter.php:125
msgid "A list of spammy or malicious sources used by email providers to filter out unwanted emails. We check your domain and IP against these lists to ensure your emails aren't flagged as spam."
msgstr ""

